+# Broadcom sources consulted
+
+Consulted 2026-08-15. The machine-readable plan follows the seed's pinned compatibility snapshot where later edits to live material could otherwise change the answer.
+
+- **Upgrade of Aria Operations 8.18.6 or 8.18.7 to VCF Operations 9.0.x is Unsupported** — Broadcom Knowledge Base, <https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/438994>. Confirmed that 8.18.6 cannot upgrade directly to 9.0.0, 9.0.1, or 9.0.2; the supported alternative is greenfield VCF Operations with custom dashboards, super metrics, views, and reports exported/imported, while historical time-series metrics do not migrate.
+- **Upgrading VMware Aria Operations 8.x to VCF Operations 9.0 using VMware Aria Suite Lifecycle** — Broadcom Knowledge Base, <https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/433805>. Confirmed the Fleet Management deployment/precheck workflow for supported Operations sources and the need to select the VCF entitlement branch.
+- **End of General Support for VMware Aria Operations 8.18** — Broadcom Knowledge Base, <https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/422643>. Confirmed the 2027-10-11 EOGS boundary for the Operations 8.18 family.
+- **End of General Support for VMware vRealize Suite 7.x** — Broadcom Knowledge Base, <https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/326048>. Confirmed that the vRealize 7.x family, including Automation, is already beyond general support and that migration to the 8.x line is the supported direction.
+- **Cumulative Update for vRealize Automation 7.6** — Broadcom Knowledge Base, <https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/325972>. Confirmed Patch 30 as the current 7.6 cumulative level and its precheck/backup prerequisites.
+- **Error when migrating a Business Group from vRA7 to vRA8 after the vRA7 certificate was updated** — Broadcom Knowledge Base, <https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/375123>. Confirmed use of the vRA 8 Migration Assistant for vRA 7 sources, business-group migration, source certificate revalidation, and re-running assessment.
+- **Aria Automation 8.18 - Error while running the Migration Assessment for vRO** — Broadcom Knowledge Base, <https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/417372>. Confirmed that Automation 8.18 assesses vRealize Orchestrator 7.6 content and that incompatible workflow content can block assessment and require remediation.
+- **How to re-trigger VCF Automation 9.0 failed upgrade workflow** — Broadcom Knowledge Base, <https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/398777>. Confirmed that Aria Automation 8.18 is imported into VCF Operations Fleet Management before creating and running the VCF Automation 9 upgrade plan.
+- **Users unable to view their existing deployments after upgrading from Aria Automation 8.18 to VCF Automation 9.0.x** — Broadcom Knowledge Base, <https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/434594>. Confirmed that deployments carry through the upgrade and that identity case normalization must be validated after the move.
+- **Upgrade Guidance for Aria Operations for Logs 8.18.x to VCF Operations for Logs 9.0.x** — Broadcom Knowledge Base, <https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/402314>. Confirmed that the Logs transition is greenfield rather than in-place, that old and new clusters run in parallel, integrations are unconfigured and reconfigured, and log-data transfer is supported for up to 90 days.
